<title>USA: Alumax Q1 dil $0.48 shr vs $1.73.</title>
<headline>Alumax Q1 dil $0.48 shr vs $1.73.</headline>
<dateline>NORCROSS, Ga. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>ALUMAX INC.</p>
<p>							Three Months Ending</p>
<p>								  March 31,</p>
<p>							   1997	  1996</p>
<p>			    (In Millions, Except Per Share Amounts)</p>
<p> Net sales					   $ 701.8    $ 802.6</p>
<p>Costs and expenses:</p>
<p>    Cost of goods sold			     545.6	630.7</p>
<p>    Selling and general			     60.9	 63.8</p>
<p>     Depreciation and amortization		37.1	 33.0</p>
<p>							   643.6	727.5</p>
<p> Earnings from operations			   58.2	 75.1</p>
<p> Gain on sales of assets(1)			    -	 78.4</p>
<p> Other income (expense), net(2)		   (.3)	 14.1</p>
<p> Interest expense, net			    (13.4)     (17.2)</p>
<p> Earnings before income taxes		     44.5	150.4</p>
<p> Income tax provision			     (17.8)     (55.0)</p>
<p> Net earnings					   26.7	 95.4</p>
<p> Preferred dividends				     -	(2.3)</p>
<p> Earnings applicable to common shares	   26.7	 93.1</p>
<p>Earnings per common share:</p>
<p>    Primary					     0.48	 2.04</p>
<p>     Fully diluted(3)				 0.48	 1.73</p>
<p>Weighted average shares in millions:</p>
<p>    Primary					     55.8	 45.5</p>
<p>     Fully diluted				    55.8	 55.2</p>
<p>Pro forma earnings per common share(4):</p>
<p>    Basic						 0.49	 2.08</p>
<p>    Diluted					     0.48	 1.73</p>
<p>(1) The three months ending March 31, 1996, includes a pretax gain of $78.4 ($48.6 after tax) related to the sale of a 23 percent interest in the Mt. Holly primary aluminum reduction plant. (2) The three months ended March 31, 1996, includes $18.6 ($18.3 after tax) for dividends received from investments in Mexican mining operations. (3) As of December 4, 1996, substantially all of the outstanding shares of the $4.00 Series A Convertible Preferred Stock was converted into the Company's Common Stock. (4) In February 1997, the Financial Accounting Standards Board issued Statement of Financial Accounting Standards No. 128, &quot;Earnings per Share&quot; (&quot;FAS 128&quot;).  The Company will adopt FAS</p>
<p>128 in the fourth quarter 1997.  The pro forma amounts presented illustrate the Company's earnings per share for the three months ended March 31, 1997, and 1996, respectively, as if FAS 128 had been adopted at the beginning of each year.</p>
